## Original Content
Over the years, you’ve probably heard at least a few people casually describe themselves as Epicureans. As used today, the label can refer to as little as enjoying the occasional expensive restaurant meal. The bar was a bit higher in the second century, as explained by ancient-history YouTuber Garrett Ryan in the new video above [&#8230;]

## Summary
The article discusses the modern misinterpretation of Epicureanism as simply enjoying fine dining, contrasting it with the original ancient philosophy. It references a video by ancient-history YouTuber Garrett Ryan explaining the historical context of the second century.

## Key Points
- Epicureanism is commonly misused today to refer to enjoying luxury experiences.
- The original Epicurean philosophy in the second century was more complex and rigorous.
- Garrett Ryan, an ancient-history YouTuber, provides educational content on the topic.


